 for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & =n\\pi  \\\\ x & =\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the zeros are $x=\\frac{n\\pi }{2},$ where $n$ is an integer." 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276306 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276307 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276308 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276309 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276310 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1041 "selection" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1104 #edb/ref 17592186276307 13194139534066 true] [17592186276305 1110 #uuid "ce6064ee-6d16-5ec2-ab67-38aae0c43702" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276306 1034 "\\frac{n\\pi }{8}" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276306 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534066 true] [17592186276306 1111 #uuid "c8dc52fc-98f0-5bc9-8fe3-92389c14490e" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276307 1034 "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276307 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534066 true] [17592186276307 1111 #uuid "5fe5fc7f-e618-516e-864d-3d6f7548060b" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276308 1034 "2\\pi n" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276308 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534066 true] [17592186276308 1111 #uuid "4e3bb7ed-b663-5998-9706-e51c7a8fa092" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276309 1034 "\\frac{n\\pi }{4}" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534066 true] [17592186276309 1111 #uuid "ead94950-c0e2-5cb3-bd4e-fc64a0c04635" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276310 1034 "4\\pi n" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534066 true] [17592186276310 1111 #uuid "52b6b85b-edd5-5a10-ae7b-35a3e9f6b321" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276311 1017 #edb/ref 17592186276312 13194139534066 true] [17592186276311 1089 "q-81557" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276311 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534066 true] [17592186276311 1100 "Which of the following expressions gives all of the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." 13194139534066 true] [17592186276311 1113 #uuid "32ece69d-c2b4-54a3-8cdb-0af4b72c6b7a" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276311 1145 "The asymptotes of $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ are given by the expression\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\nTo find the asymptotes of $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}),$ we replace the $x$ on the left-hand side of the above with $(\\frac{\\pi x}{2}).$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi x}{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi .\n$$\n\nSolving for $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\pi x}{2} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}+n \\\\ x & =1+2n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the expression giving all the vertical asymptotes is $x=1+2n,$ where $n$ is an integer." 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276313 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276314 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276315 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276316 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1000 #edb/ref 17592186276317 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1041 "selection" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1104 #edb/ref 17592186276316 13194139534066 true] [17592186276312 1110 #uuid "9d25ae64-a58a-5566-9862-d970b871c7d0" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276313 1034 "x=2+n" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534066 true] [17592186276313 1111 #uuid "ad233bc5-bfa0-5d47-9ba5-258600819bb8" 13194139534066 true] [17592186276314 1034 "x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi " 13194139534066 true] [17592186276314 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534066 true] [17592186276314 11